{
	"info": {
		"name": "Bet Room and Votes Service API",
		"description": "Drives a full duel in the order the widget does: alice opens a room from a bet she has already placed, bob holds a seat and confirms it with his own, then alice offers a rematch only bob can take.\n\nRun the requests top to bottom — each one saves what the next needs into the environment. A pre-request script on the collection mints fresh bet references per run, because one bet can belong to at most one room.\n\nAUTHENTICATION: with AUTH_JWT_SECRET unset the server takes the bearer token itself as the caller's identity, which is what makes aliceToken/bobToken/carolToken three different people here. Set the secret and these need to be real HS256 tokens whose `sub` claim identifies the caller.\n\nThe tests assert the three wire-format facts that break the widget silently: success bodies are not enveloped, error bodies use `message` rather than `error`, and every timestamp is epoch milliseconds.\n\nThe final requests cover the free vote (`/votes*`), which is a separate surface with its own contract in `docs/votes-api.md`. They run on their own event id so a re-run starts from an unvoted market, and they assert the three things that break the widget silently: keys come back exactly as they were sent, a changed pick is refused with its own `alreadyVoted` code, and the counts response carries nothing about the caller.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "baseUrl",
			"value": "http://localhost:5000"
		},
		{
			"key": "voteEventId",
			"value": ""
		},
		{
			"key": "voteDeviceToken",
			"value": ""
		}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Ping (public)",
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ping",
					"host": [
						"{{baseUrl}}"
					],
					"path": [
						"ping"
					]
				},
				"description": "Liveness. One of only two routes that need no credential."
			},
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
						]
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Limits without a credential -> 401",
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms/limits",
					"host": [
						"{{baseUrl}}"
					],
					"path": [
						"rooms",
						"limits"
					]
				},
				"description": "Every room route needs a bearer credential: the payload carries no user identifier, so an unauthenticated request cannot be attributed to anyone."
			},
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"pm.test('status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
							"const body = pm.response.json();",
							"// The widget reads body.message and falls back to the HTTP status text.",
							"pm.test('error body uses message, not error', () => {",
							"  pm.expect(body.message).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
							"  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('error');",
							"});"
						]
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Get limits",
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "Authorization",
